        "original_id": "a4b6c542-23a3-5bdc-b148-8985e0132ff2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: NASA, DOE, North American Carbon Program\n- People: Wernher von Braun\n- Projects: Applications Technology Satellites, ATS-2, Project Vulcan\n- Products: V-2 rocket, Saturn V\n- Places: Cape Canaveral\n- Systems: Atlas-Agena D rocket\n- Concepts: fossil fuel carbon dioxide emissions\n\nFacts:\n- Wernher von Braun was born on March 23, 1912, and died on June 16, 1977.\n- Wernher von Braun was a German, later American, aerospace engineer and space architect.\n- Wernher von Braun is credited with inventing the V-2 rocket for Nazi Germany and the Saturn V for the United States.\n- The Applications Technology Satellites were a series of experimental satellites launched by NASA under the supervision of, among others, Wernher von Braun.\n- ATS-2 was an Applications Technology Satellite communications satellite launched by NASA on April 6, 1967.\n- ATS-2 was launched on an Atlas-Agena D rocket from Cape Canaveral.\n- Project Vulcan is a NASA and DOE funded effort under the North American Carbon Program.\n- Project Vulcan aims to quantify North American fossil fuel carbon dioxide emissions at much finer space and time scales than had previously been achieved.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5713f163-3d93-5c85-8150-8684300e1726",
        "text": "Page: Applications Technology Satellite. Sentence: The Applications Technology Satellites (ATS) were a series of experimental satellites launched by NASA, under the supervision of, among others, Wernher von Braun.\nPage: Wernher von Braun. Sentence: Wernher Magnus Maximilian Freiherr von Braun (March 23, 1912 – June 16, 1977) was a German, later American, aerospace engineer and space architect credited with inventing the V-2 rocket for Nazi Germany and the Saturn V for the United States.\nPage: ATS-2. Sentence: ATS-2 (Applications Technology Satellite) was a communications satellite launched by NASA on April 6, 1967 on an Atlas-Agena D rocket from Cape Canaveral.\nPage: Project Vulcan. Sentence: Project Vulcan is a NASA/DOE funded effort under the North American Carbon Program (NACP) to quantify North American fossil fuel carbon dioxide (CO) emissions at space/time scales much finer than has been achieved in the past.",
